Syntax: cast 'fear' <target>

The Fear spell overwhelms the victim's mind with supernatural terror,
causing them to instantly flee from the caster in blind panic. For the
duration of the effect, the caster's mere presence induces paralyzing
dread, preventing the victim from willingly approaching.

Victims who fail their saving throw will:
  - Immediately flee the room in a random direction
  - Be unable to return to the caster's location while affected
  - Panic and act erratically if cornered

The fear effect lasts for a duration dependent on the caster's level.
Strong-willed creatures have a chance to resist the initial spell and
may shake off the effect more quickly.

Fear cannot be cast on oneself. Creatures that recover from fear and
survive often bear lasting grudges against those who terrorized them.

See Also: HYPNOSIS, CALM, INTIMIDATE
